# 1-SP JPEG position hints (personalised, PNG-only)

Supervisor 2026-09-22: On duplicate-order SKU files in the **single** folder only, a JPEG next to the main PNG is a **position hint**, not a second design.

- Queue only the PNG. Never place the JPEG on the canvas.
- Hint only if the matching main PNG exists. JPEG-only → do not invent a design; fall through to double as today.
- Tokens: dedicated hyphen segment `-P-` / `-S-` / `-S1-` / `-S2-` / `-SL-` / `-SR-` before the full SKU. Do not treat apparel size `S` inside the SKU as sleeve. Build stems; do not substring-scan.
- Token order: S1, S2, SL, SR, P, S (longer sleeve tokens before plain S). First hit wins. One PNG, one size.
- `-P-` JPEG → 80×100 (including kids). Sleeve tokens → 100×100. Not the legacy kids 65×80 path.
- Legacy `{OrderNumber}-P.png` / `-S.png` / `-S1.png` / `-S2.png` / `-SL.png` / `-SR.png` stays (unique orders). Kids `-K-` → 65×80 on that PNG-suffix path.
- Main search stays PNG-only (`IMAGE_EXTENSIONS = ['.png']`). Do not expand to JPEG.
- Hint lookup only when `is_duplicate_order`, `position` is None, and a single-folder PNG was found.
- Missing Logo inherits via `process_personalised_designs`. Do not duplicate in the GUI.
- Token tables live in `scripts/src/core/sku_position_hints.py` (no I/O). Do not import I/O from `image_resizing`.
